[section, $md:
    # Moth Patterns

    A Moth application grows from ordinary values, functions, templates and
    modules. These guides show how to combine them into larger projects without
    introducing a separate component language or framework.

    The examples describe Moth's **final design**. Some parts are planned rather
    than implemented. Use the @../progress (progress matrix) for current support
    and the @../cheatsheet (language cheatsheet) for the intended syntax.

    ## Explore the patterns

    1. @./websites/ (Website structure) - organize entries, modules, shared
       packages and authored content across a site.
    2. @./components/ (HTML components) - assemble reusable HTML values with
       templates, const functions and explicit resource dependencies.
    3. @./browser-behaviour/ (Browser behaviour) - add typed DOM operations and,
       later, events without embedding JavaScript in components.

    Start with website structure, then follow the component and browser guides.
    Each guide has a short Basic view and a deeper Advanced view explaining the
    design choices.

    ## Beyond websites

    The same separation of computation, reusable values, capabilities and
    entry-owned work also guides future interactive applications and other
    project builders. HTML is our first concrete example, not a new language
    boundary.
]

